+// The logo is placed the way `kitten icat --unicode-placeholder` places one: the image is
+// transmitted as a virtual placement (U=1) and then referenced by a grid of U+10EEEE cells whose
+// foreground colour carries the image id and whose combining marks carry the cell's row and column
+// in the image. Nothing depends on where a terminal leaves the cursor after a graphics command,
+// and the grid is ordinary text, so the logo scrolls with the buffer and is redrawn from the
+// stored image by anything that repaints those cells — tmux, an editor, a resize.
